      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5fca5df4d58780532024a52b|full_name}: Im aware of the fact that it's only on the first switch where world builders need to wait awhile (To convert Windows to android). However that's not the issue i'm trying to bring up here. \n\nThe issue im pointing out here is the fact that *AFTER* you switch from windows to android. Theres an \"AUTO FIX\" button that converts ALL your textures in your project files to ASTC. Depending on your project file this can take a matter of 30min to a matter of even hours. - This is because instead just converting the needed textures in the scene (The ones that will be used in the Android build of the world) The *AUTO FIX*, button converts ALL unity project textures to ASTC.\n\nThis is where my issue is- Why does it need to convert every single texture in the unity project to ASTC when only certain textures are used in the scene?\n\nI may have been too unclear with my initial post- I hope this helps.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
