      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I now realized I worded this very poorly and cant seem to edit the post anymore. Reposting my answer to DrBlackRat here.\n\nThe issue im pointing out here is the fact that AFTER you switch from windows to android. Theres an \"AUTO FIX\" button that converts ALL your textures in your project files to ASTC. Depending on your project file this can take a matter of 30min to a matter of even hours. - This is because instead just converting the needed textures in the scene (The ones that will be used in the Android build of the world) The AUTO FIX, button converts ALL unity project textures to ASTC.\n\nThis is where my issue is- Why does it need to convert every single texture in the unity project to ASTC when only certain textures are used in the scene?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
